<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
	Vara is intentionally NOT sandboxed (no com.apple.security.app-sandbox).

	App Sandbox is fundamentally incompatible with Vara's core mechanics:
	  - global keyboard monitoring via a CGEventTap (system-wide hotkey),
	  - synthetic Cmd+V paste into the frontmost app of the user's choice,
	  - spawning the local Python Hviske speech runtime as a child process,
	  - connecting to arbitrary user-chosen LLM endpoints (Groq, OpenAI,
	    Ollama/DGX on the LAN, etc.).

	Enabling the sandbox would break these features and the product itself,
	so it is deliberately omitted. Note: because the app is not sandboxed,
	any "Helt privat / Completely private" UI copy must be softened to
	truthful wording (handled by the UI layer, not this entitlements file).

	Only the microphone entitlement below is required.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
